  "internal_thinking": "I am currently at 4 victory points and need only one more settlement to reach the winning 5 points. I have a road already built to node 23, which is a valid settlement spot. To build there, I need 1 wood, 1 brick, 1 wheat, and 1 sheep. My current resources are 3 wood and 2 wheat. I am missing brick and sheep. I have a 3:1 port at node 9, which means I could trade 3 wood for either a brick or a sheep, but not both this turn. Ziv and Shon are actively blocking me because they know I'm one settlement away from winning. Ziv has sheep but rejected my trades. Shon has brick production but is hostile. Given that a 7 was just rolled and my trade offers were rejected, I cannot win this turn. However, I have a high probability of winning on my next turn: a roll of 4 (wood+sheep), 5 (sheep), 6 (brick), or 10 (brick) would provide the missing pieces or enough wood to use my 3:1 port for the win. I will end my turn now and try to deflect the table's focus toward Shon's wheat-heavy position.",
